      "summary": "This GitHub repository contains a lightweight transformerbased language model implemented in Python using PyTorch. Trained locally on the Tiny Shakespeare dataset, the model demonstrates modern architectural features such as RMSNorm, Rotary Positional Embeddings, Grouped Query Attention, SwiGLU feedforward networks, and weight tying. It consists of four transformer layers with a total of approximately 2.76 million parameters, designed to predict the next character in text sequences. The project includes a detailed architecture overview, training pipeline, and sample training progress, showcasing how to build and train a smallscale language model from scratch. It serves as an educational example of core transformer components and language modeling techniques, suitable for learning and experimentation.",
